"O'odee are ground-dwelling, ostrich-like Artonan birds known for their laugh-like calls."
"Adults have long tendril-like tail feathers, scaled legs and claws; chicks are bubble-eyed."
"Their eggs, like pale basketballs, lie in dips in spongy plant clumps; they eat moths and worms."
"They are not territorial and are farmed in desert villages."
